      "source": [
        "### D14. Parse one messy line, step by step\n",
        "\n",
        "Start with `raw_line = \"  Srv-01 , used=87 , total=100  \"`.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. `.strip()` the whole line.\n",
        "2. Split off the hostname with `.split(\",\", 1)` into `hostname_part` and `rest`.\n",
        "3. Clean the hostname with `.strip().lower()`.\n",
        "4. Split `rest` on `\",\"`. For each piece, split on `\"=\"`, strip the key and the value, and convert the\n",
        "   value with `float()`.\n",
        "5. Put everything into one dict and print it.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Expected output:** `{'hostname': 'srv-01', 'used': 87.0, 'total': 100.0}`"
      ],
      "id": "HW32QsGNaz8U"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "LPpTAUrJaz8U"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "raw_line = \"  Srv-01 , used=87 , total=100  \"\n",
        "\n",
        "line = raw_line.strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "hostname_part, rest = line.split(\",\", 1)\n",
        "\n",
        "hostname = hostname_part.strip().lower()\n",
        "\n",
        "fields = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for piece in rest.split(\",\"):\n",
        "    key, value = piece.split(\"=\")\n",
        "    fields[key.strip().lower()] = float(value.strip())\n",
        "\n",
        "record = {\n",
        "    \"hostname\": hostname,\n",
        "    \"used\": fields[\"used\"],\n",
        "    \"total\": fields[\"total\"]\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "print(record)"
      ],
      "id": "LPpTAUrJaz8U"
    },
